WEBVTT

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:24.370
Hey!

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:28.990
I-If...

00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:34.490
If I lose... If I lose to you in this
competition, I'll quite figure skating!

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:38.740
I swear! Don't forget it!

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:44.740
All-Japan Novice Championships!

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:49.830
The performer on ice right now
is Kensei Maeshima, a fifth grader!

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:12.990
He successfully landed an axel jump!

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:15.370
That was wonderful.

00:01:15.370 --> 00:01:17.620
Reo Shinozaki is currently in first place.

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:20.700
There's a wide gap in their scores,
but Maeshima can still turn the tables!

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:26.830
Maeshima lost his parents, who were
former pro skaters and also his coaches,

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:30.870
in a car accident two months ago.
He's here after overcoming that grief.

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:35.080
He's always lost to Shinozaki
in previous championships.

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:38.200
He must be more determined than ever before.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:41.120
It shows in his performance.

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:45.740
Grandma. Grandpa. I'm sorry
for worrying you all this time.

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:50.240
But if I get first place,
I'm sure I can ease their minds.

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:52.200
I can skate more!

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:06.160
He landed his jumps perfectly.

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:08.990
Now, what will his score be?!

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:11.610
What?

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:15.120
Oh, wow! He was just 0.30 points shy!

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:19.040
The champion is, once again, Reo Shinozaki!

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:22.740
I practiced so hard...

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:29.200
But... I know I don't know
when to give up... I know it's lame.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:32.830
But... But if he...

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:36.830
Shinozaki.

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:41.240
If he acknowledges me as his rival...

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:43.370
You beat me again.

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:45.870
...I'd like to continue...

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:48.120
But next time, I'm definitely gonna--

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:49.700
The results are out.

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:54.370
You'll never be able to beat me.

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:58.620
You’re just wasting your time.

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:01.490
"Boy Prodigy"
"Reo Shinozaki (11)"

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:04.040
"Reo Shinozaki (13)"
"Junior Championships"
"Victory"

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:06.540
"Training Camp"
"Shinozaki"
"Perfectly Calm"

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:08.950
"No One in Japan Can Beat Him"
"Wins Another Championship"

00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:13.240
Shinozaki, you've won the Japan
Championships four times in a row.

00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:16.660
Why are you switching to skate-leading?

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:18.950
This was my plan all along.

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:21.660
I've already submitted
the paperwork to the Federation.

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:25.450
People expected you to debut at
the Seniors now that you're in high school.

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:27.990
What made you decide to do this instead?

00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:31.830
This decision was needed
in order for me to grow.

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:34.620
Many of your rivals from
your elementary school days

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:36.790
have switched to skate-leading.

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:40.290
Are you looking forward to seeing
and competing against them again?

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:42.410
I'm not interested in that.

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:47.950
As an athlete, in skate-leading as well...

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:49.790
I'll aim for the top.

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:52.240
Hmph.

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:25.490
Episode 1

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:25.490
Pact

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:39.080
Oof.

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:41.490
You beat us!

00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:44.120
You really should join the
basketball club, Maeshima.

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:46.330
You'd be chosen as a regular member right away.

00:05:46.330 --> 00:05:49.160
No way. I hate practicing.

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:53.160
Get out! Then how come you can move like that?

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:56.080
You can find pro basketball videos
and stuff like that online, right?

00:05:56.080 --> 00:06:01.830
Average people can't imitate or adapt
movements by just watching them!

00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:03.540
Thanks!

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:06.120
Come to think of it, you said
the same thing before.

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:06.670
Hm?

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:08.950
Remember? During the baseball game,

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:12.040
you said you copied a
pro ballplayer from an old video.

00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:15.410
Didn't you say that's how you
learned how to play soccer, too?

00:06:15.410 --> 00:06:19.410
I remember the baseball and soccer clubs
were trying hard to recruit you.

00:06:19.410 --> 00:06:22.830
But when you got cocky and
challenged the go and shogi clubs,

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:26.490
you got thrashed.

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:27.620
Shut up.

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:29.410
You're wasting your talent.

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:33.290
Unlike us, who go home after school,
you should join a club.

00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:36.740
No, thanks. I only wanna do the fun stuff.

00:06:36.740 --> 00:06:39.370
Like playing in a match to stand out.

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:40.240
Oh?

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:42.490
Aren't they the skate-leading club?

00:06:42.490 --> 00:06:47.910
Sorry! I can help any club <i>except</i>
skating-related clubs, unfortunately...

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:58.810
"First-Aid Kit"

00:06:47.910 --> 00:06:51.830
Even if we used to be in the same club before.

00:06:51.830 --> 00:06:53.740
I wasn't in the same club!

00:06:53.740 --> 00:06:54.580
Hey.

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:56.370
Okay, okay.

00:06:56.370 --> 00:06:58.990
Maeshima. What are you talking about?

00:06:58.990 --> 00:06:59.830
Hm?

00:06:59.830 --> 00:07:03.200
No one in our club is inferior to you.

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:05.370
We'll never ask for your help.

00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:06.790
Good to know.

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:09.870
So you said, but the truth is,
you wanna skate with us, don’t you?

00:07:09.870 --> 00:07:11.990
People had such high expectations of you.

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:14.950
It was you who chose to be how you are now.

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:16.870
U-Um... Captain...

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:21.160
Maeshima. I hate you. I really hate you.

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:23.830
If you don't wanna take part in skate-leading,

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:26.490
then don't act like we're childhood
friends with that frivolous atti--

00:07:26.490 --> 00:07:29.490
Oh, don't snap like that, jeez...

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:32.330
See you later, Maeshima.

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:33.910
Yeah, see ya!

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:41.200
Sorry. I gotta go to the restroom.

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:44.040
Huh? We're about to clear this level.

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:45.200
Look behind you.

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:46.740
Hm?

00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:52.490
Figure Skating

00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:52.490
Shinozaki Switches to Skate-Leading

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:48.790
Jeez, he's so mentally weak...

00:07:48.790 --> 00:07:50.120
Despite what he says,

00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:52.910
he never talks about his
elementary school days, you know.

00:07:55.290 --> 00:07:56.990
How lame...

00:07:56.990 --> 00:07:59.240
With Shinozaki switching from figure skating,

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:01.490
skate-leading has entered the spotlight.

00:08:01.490 --> 00:08:05.040
Here we'll explain what kind of sport it is.

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:03.670
Skate-Leading

00:08:03.670 --> 00:08:04.630
Skate-Leading

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:08.160
Skate-leading is also called
"team figure skating."

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:11.040
Five members skate as a team in three positions.

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:15.050
Lead

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:14.990
"Leads" are point-getters who
perform many jump combinations.

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:19.560
Wing

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:19.560
Wing

00:08:14.990 --> 00:08:19.540
"Wings" are often agile skaters who
get lifted in moves such as the twist lift.

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:23.060
Guard

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:23.060
Guard

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:22.990
"Guards" offer support for
performances such as lifts and steps.

00:08:22.990 --> 00:08:27.370
Teams have to have at least
one skater for each position.

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:33.830
But five people stake at the same time, right?

00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:36.120
Judges must have a hard time judging.

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:39.370
Right. That's where this automatic
measurement system comes in.

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:41.580
This system uses a total of 15 cameras and...

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:43.870
"Manager"
"Answer" "Decline"

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:52.120
What is it? This better not
be about skate-leading...

00:08:55.370 --> 00:08:56.290
See ya!

00:08:56.290 --> 00:08:57.160
Later!

00:08:57.160 --> 00:08:58.200
Yeah.

00:09:03.240 --> 00:09:06.910
Excuse me. Can I ask you for directions?

00:09:06.910 --> 00:09:08.540
Oh, sure. Where do you wanna go?

00:09:08.540 --> 00:09:11.870
Thank you! I moved to this area recently.

00:09:11.870 --> 00:09:14.200
I don't want people to think that I'm a bumpkin,

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:16.990
but then I don't know my way around at all.

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:19.700
To think the first person
I talked to was so nice...!

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:20.790
I'm really glad I mustered up the courage and--

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:23.120
Okay, okay! I get it.

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:25.120
So where do you wanna go?

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:29.950
Right. The rink Ionodai High's
skate-leading club uses for practices,

00:09:29.950 --> 00:09:33.160
and the rink Reo Shinozaki
uses for his practices.

00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:35.290
Sorry. Ask someone else.

00:09:35.290 --> 00:09:38.200
Oh, don't be so coldhearted...

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:44.410
Kensei Maeshima, past runner-up
of the All-Japan Novice Championships.

00:09:49.330 --> 00:09:53.120
Just watch this. Someone uploaded it.

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:56.450
I heard that this is Shinozaki's
next exhibition program.

00:09:57.990 --> 00:09:59.870
He really is good, isn't he?

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:02.330
His movements are so sharp.

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:04.740
It made me want to see it in person.

00:10:04.740 --> 00:10:06.660
What's your problem?!

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:10.990
If you're just a fan, look it up
on your phone and go by yourself!

00:10:12.290 --> 00:10:13.790
He's biting.

00:10:18.990 --> 00:10:21.990
Grandpa, I'm gonna head out for some roadwork.

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:38.200
As I thought, he does tighten
his muscles here... which means...

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:47.490
Hm? This is strange... I wonder
if it's because I'm on the ground...

00:10:47.490 --> 00:10:51.620
On the actual ice, I guess I have to push
more with the back outside edge, huh?

00:10:51.620 --> 00:10:53.700
How do I take off...?

00:10:53.700 --> 00:10:56.410
I have to use the right side more as an axis,
or I'll land on the wrong spot.

00:10:56.410 --> 00:10:58.660
Which means...

00:10:58.660 --> 00:11:00.040
How was that?!

00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:02.490
I do acknowledge your effort.

00:11:02.490 --> 00:11:06.660
But you bend forward when you jump.

00:11:06.660 --> 00:11:09.660
That's why your left leg becomes unstable.

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:12.370
You should stop training only on the ground.

00:11:12.370 --> 00:11:14.450
What's with you?!

00:11:14.450 --> 00:11:17.700
Are you actually stalking me
instead of Shinozaki?

00:11:17.700 --> 00:11:20.120
I'm gonna report you to the police.

00:11:20.120 --> 00:11:22.370
Go right ahead.

00:11:22.370 --> 00:11:25.910
But you sure about that? If you do,
your grandparents will find out

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:29.370
that you've been practicing
figure skating every day.

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:35.290
The distance this park is from your house
means you're hiding it from them, right?

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:37.330
Maybe you don't wanna worry them?

00:11:37.330 --> 00:11:40.660
You ran into me earlier on purpose, didn't you?

00:11:42.790 --> 00:11:45.120
Who are you?

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:46.990
What do you want?

00:11:46.990 --> 00:11:52.040
Sorry that I didn't introduce myself yet.
My name is Hayato Sasugai.

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:55.990
I'm Reo Shinozaki's younger half-brother.

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:08.490
What? What'd you say?

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:10.620
Shinozaki's younger brother?

00:12:10.620 --> 00:12:15.160
Yup. In any case, my old man
sure is lame, isn't he?

00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:17.580
Shinozaki and I are the same age.

00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:20.200
He was just born a little earlier than I was.

00:12:20.200 --> 00:12:22.120
So why is someone like you here?

00:12:22.120 --> 00:12:24.240
Revenge.

00:12:24.240 --> 00:12:29.370
To me, Shinozaki is seriously
an eyesore and a pain in the neck.

00:12:29.370 --> 00:12:31.700
He's always in front of me.

00:12:31.700 --> 00:12:36.700
No matter what he does,
he always stands above me without fail...

00:12:36.700 --> 00:12:40.490
...with that condescendingly cold look in his eyes.

00:12:40.490 --> 00:12:42.620
That sounds familiar to you, too, right?

00:12:42.620 --> 00:12:45.200
You'll never be able to beat me.

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:48.120
You should quit figure skating.

00:12:48.120 --> 00:12:52.290
When I finally found a place where I
could belong, he impudently marched into it.

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:53.080
A place where you could belong?

00:12:53.080 --> 00:12:55.830
I'm talking about skate-leading.

00:12:55.830 --> 00:13:01.950
But then, I thought it was a good chance
to bring him down from his throne.

00:13:01.950 --> 00:13:05.540
Fortunately, this town has
a powerhouse--Ionodai High.

00:13:05.540 --> 00:13:07.990
And most of all, there's you.

00:13:07.990 --> 00:13:10.910
Based on my calculations,
you guys would be the strongest team.

00:13:10.910 --> 00:13:14.290
Sorry, but I quit skating ages ag--

00:13:14.290 --> 00:13:17.080
Come back and stand on the ice, Maeshima!

00:13:18.660 --> 00:13:22.240
What're you saying? "Come back"?

00:13:24.790 --> 00:13:27.580
I need you!

00:13:27.580 --> 00:13:30.160
You came all the way here to say that to me?

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:32.120
"The strongest team"?

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:34.580
Are you trying to use me
as a tool for your revenge?

00:13:34.580 --> 00:13:38.740
If you want revenge that badly, then why
don't you skate and lead the team yourse--

00:13:38.740 --> 00:13:40.830
I can't jump anymore.

00:13:42.540 --> 00:13:44.660
I had surgery many times.

00:13:44.660 --> 00:13:48.490
I can walk, but I can't go back on the ice.

00:13:48.490 --> 00:13:51.950
But I'm just like you.

00:13:51.950 --> 00:13:54.540
There's something I can't give up on.

00:13:54.540 --> 00:13:58.490
You have something like that,
too, right? I know you do!

00:13:58.490 --> 00:14:02.870
Right now, I'm aiming to become
a skate-leading coach.

00:14:02.870 --> 00:14:07.790
My current goal is to coach the
national team for world competitions.

00:14:07.790 --> 00:14:10.490
The fit's not adjusted,
but they should be in your size.

00:14:10.490 --> 00:14:12.160
What? They're for me?

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:17.120
I think you know this, but Shinozaki will
perform his last exhibition this weekend.

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:19.830
Memorize what's in the video
and come to the venue.

00:14:19.830 --> 00:14:21.620
I'll get you a slot to perform.

00:14:21.620 --> 00:14:25.200
Let's raise the beacon of your
comeback in front of Shinozaki.

00:14:25.200 --> 00:14:27.790
Screw that! Why would I go?!

00:14:27.790 --> 00:14:31.200
Do you know the phrase
"Take time by the forelock"?

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:35.370
Or do you like spending
the rest of your life in regret?

00:14:40.950 --> 00:14:43.830
Take it from someone with experience.

00:14:43.830 --> 00:14:47.620
If you keep lying to yourself,
your mind will be torn,

00:14:47.620 --> 00:14:50.700
and someday, you won't even
know your own true feelings.

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:00.490
"Junior Figure Skating Championships"

00:15:03.580 --> 00:15:06.200
Captain. The competition is over. Can I go home?

00:15:06.200 --> 00:15:09.040
No, you can't. What do you
think we came here for?

00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:11.740
Watch Shinozaki carefully, Himekawa.

00:15:11.740 --> 00:15:14.580
He'll probably skate the same position as you.

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:16.450
You're our team's ace,
so he'll be your opponent.

00:15:16.450 --> 00:15:19.950
He's the ace? I'm the ace, right? Ace!

00:15:19.950 --> 00:15:21.790
Be quiet.

00:15:21.790 --> 00:15:25.580
Personality-wise, he's the most
suited for it on our team, though.

00:15:25.580 --> 00:15:27.330
Thank you for waiting!

00:15:27.330 --> 00:15:29.370
In the following exhibition program,

00:15:29.370 --> 00:15:30.950
you'll see a performance by Reo Shinozaki

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:35.120
who will switch to high school
skate-leading after this!

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:44.830
Screw that!

00:15:44.830 --> 00:15:46.580
Dammit!

00:15:49.700 --> 00:15:51.990
I...!

00:16:14.330 --> 00:16:18.330
I didn't give it up to be mocked
by a guy like that!

00:16:21.870 --> 00:16:23.040
I can...

00:16:25.370 --> 00:16:26.700
I can...

00:16:29.580 --> 00:16:31.790
I can still jump!

00:16:31.790 --> 00:16:33.740
I can skate more!

00:16:38.540 --> 00:16:40.660
Are you warmed up enough?

00:16:44.540 --> 00:16:48.620
What, did you come all this way
to complain about the other day?

00:16:50.080 --> 00:16:53.240
What a wonderful last exhibition
performance by Shinozaki!

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:56.910
We can't help but look forward
to his performance in skate-leading as well!

00:16:56.910 --> 00:16:59.870
Shinozaki is on a perfect skater's path.

00:16:59.870 --> 00:17:02.290
Please give him a hand again!

00:17:00.240 --> 00:17:02.290
Skaters Waiting Room F

00:17:05.540 --> 00:17:06.370
Hey.

00:17:06.370 --> 00:17:09.290
Don't worry. This room is for trainees.

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:10.330
But that guy--

00:17:10.330 --> 00:17:13.740
I've settled up with his friends, so it's okay.

00:17:13.740 --> 00:17:15.790
His skating is just passable anyway.

00:17:15.790 --> 00:17:17.620
But that's not an excuse for me to skate.

00:17:17.620 --> 00:17:20.120
Then what'd you come here for?

00:17:20.120 --> 00:17:22.870
You've got ice skates in that bag, right?

00:17:22.870 --> 00:17:25.910
I recognized your talent.
So have confidence in yourself.

00:17:25.910 --> 00:17:28.740
You have unbelievable dynamic and kinetic vision

00:17:28.740 --> 00:17:32.540
and an aptitude that allows you to move
your body close to how you imagine,

00:17:32.540 --> 00:17:34.370
which is rare.

00:17:34.370 --> 00:17:36.790
Who cares about the past?

00:17:36.790 --> 00:17:40.910
You're the only one who's hung up on his pride.

00:17:40.910 --> 00:17:42.160
And from fifth grade, too.

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:43.660
I was just--!

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:46.990
Stop whining. Show off
what you've got on the ice.

00:17:46.990 --> 00:17:50.120
The second half will start soon
now that the rink has been resurfaced.

00:17:50.120 --> 00:17:53.200
We'll dim the lighting before
the performances start,

00:17:52.120 --> 00:17:53.950
Reo

00:17:53.200 --> 00:17:56.120
so please watch your step
coming back to your seat.

00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:03.240
Sit down. Watch it until the end.
That's just polite.

00:18:03.240 --> 00:18:06.870
What're you saying? You saw
Shinozaki's performance earlier.

00:18:06.870 --> 00:18:08.580
If he performs at that level in skate-leading...

00:18:08.580 --> 00:18:12.370
We can't just sit around. We have
to get practicing right away.

00:18:12.370 --> 00:18:13.580
Terauchi.

00:18:16.620 --> 00:18:20.910
That damn Sasugai...
How dare he run his mouth like that...

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:23.870
And this program...!

00:18:23.870 --> 00:18:25.540
Well, who cares?

00:18:25.540 --> 00:18:28.950
I skate because I want to.
That's all that matters now.

00:18:28.950 --> 00:18:36.460
"Junior Figure Skating Championships"

00:18:28.950 --> 00:18:31.120
You get it, right, Maeshima?

00:18:31.120 --> 00:18:34.120
It all depends on how well you can copy him.

00:18:34.120 --> 00:18:36.870
Excuse me, about this program change...

00:18:36.870 --> 00:18:42.370
Oh, it's okay. Yamada wanted it
to be a surprise for Shinozaki.

00:18:42.370 --> 00:18:45.200
You know, he's Kuonji's friend, so...

00:19:04.990 --> 00:19:07.790
Oh? This is different from his planned program.

00:19:07.790 --> 00:19:10.660
Isn't this the music Shinozaki used?

00:19:13.410 --> 00:19:16.410
Now, show us, Maeshima.

00:19:23.580 --> 00:19:26.120
Huh? The same music Shinozaki used...?

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:28.450
Hey, hey... Even the routine is the same?

00:19:28.450 --> 00:19:31.580
This is nonsense! No one told us about this!

00:19:43.830 --> 00:19:48.290
Don't be afraid of making mistakes.
You haven't been on the rink in a while.

00:19:48.290 --> 00:19:51.450
Damn... Damn...

00:19:51.450 --> 00:19:53.790
What's this...?

00:19:53.790 --> 00:19:55.790
This is fun.

00:19:56.910 --> 00:20:02.450
Oh, that's right! I'm back... in the rink!

00:20:02.450 --> 00:20:06.950
I can do a lot more on ice! I can jump more!

00:20:06.950 --> 00:20:10.870
Is that really Yamada?
His skills are really rough.

00:20:10.870 --> 00:20:15.490
But he's got good instincts. I like it.

00:20:15.490 --> 00:20:18.580
Once... Just once is enough.

00:20:18.580 --> 00:20:20.950
Show off what you’ve got to everyone here.

00:20:20.950 --> 00:20:23.950
Then the path will open up!

00:20:23.950 --> 00:20:25.120
Now!

00:20:29.580 --> 00:20:30.740
What?!

00:20:32.450 --> 00:20:35.290
Was that a quadruple?! What a surprise!

00:20:35.290 --> 00:20:38.120
Yamada is performing exactly the same program!

00:20:38.120 --> 00:20:41.450
Isn't this the first time
we've seen a quadruple flip?!

00:20:41.450 --> 00:20:45.200
That bastard added some stuff on his own!

00:20:56.540 --> 00:20:59.540
Maeshima. You're like a dog.

00:20:59.540 --> 00:21:01.200
When you're happy, you jump too much.

00:21:01.200 --> 00:21:02.410
Shut up.

00:21:02.410 --> 00:21:05.990
It stirred your soul, didn't it?

00:21:05.990 --> 00:21:09.330
Deep inside, I've probably
wanted to do it this whole time.

00:21:09.330 --> 00:21:12.330
Then we have a deal on teaming up?

00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:14.540
I'll take you to the top.

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:16.950
Stop acting so high and mighty.

00:21:16.950 --> 00:21:18.910
Hey, you two!

00:21:18.910 --> 00:21:21.540
You guys're the ones who lied
and locked me up, right?!

00:21:21.540 --> 00:21:22.370
What?!

00:21:22.370 --> 00:21:24.160
Now, now. You want money? I can pay you.

00:21:24.160 --> 00:21:28.160
That's not the point! Someone! Catch them!

00:21:28.160 --> 00:21:30.240
You bastard! What's the deal?!

00:21:30.240 --> 00:21:31.490
Sorry!

00:21:31.490 --> 00:21:33.790
H-Huh?! Y-Your foot!

00:21:33.790 --> 00:21:36.700
It was special effects makeup.

00:21:36.700 --> 00:21:37.830
What?!

00:21:39.450 --> 00:21:42.200
You dummy. Don't laugh so hard.

00:21:46.540 --> 00:21:51.330
So, I, Kensei Maeshima,
goofed around a lot yesterday,

00:21:51.330 --> 00:21:55.540
but I'm going to formally join
the skate-leading club! Thank you!

00:21:53.490 --> 00:21:55.540
"Club Sign-up Form"

00:21:57.160 --> 00:21:59.120
Joining the club? Now?

00:21:59.120 --> 00:22:02.620
Don't assume it's okay just because we've
known each other since elementary school.

00:22:02.620 --> 00:22:06.040
There's no place for you in our club.

00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:51.030
Next Time

00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:51.030
Break

00:23:37.290 --> 00:23:37.850
Captain.

00:23:37.850 --> 00:23:38.310
Hm?

00:23:38.310 --> 00:23:38.930
Captain.

00:23:38.930 --> 00:23:39.290
Hm?

00:23:39.290 --> 00:23:40.100
Captain!

00:23:40.100 --> 00:23:40.450
Hm?

00:23:40.450 --> 00:23:41.690
Captain Terauchi.

00:23:41.690 --> 00:23:41.990
Hm?

00:23:41.990 --> 00:23:42.690
Sho!

00:23:42.690 --> 00:23:44.660
What is it, Maeshima?

00:23:44.660 --> 00:23:47.160
Terauchi... I can't believe you...

00:23:47.160 --> 00:23:50.990
What? Did I do something wrong...?
